public List<RGB> GetUniqueColors(List<RGB> allColors, int numberOfColorsToSelect)
{
    Random random = new Random();
    List<RGB> selectedColors = new List<RGB>();
    for (int i = 0; i < numberOfColorsToSelect; i++)
    {
        selectedColors.Add(allColors[i]);
    }
    for (int i = numberOfColorsToSelect; i < allColors.Count; i++)
    {
        int randomIndex = random.Next(i + 1);
        if (randomIndex < numberOfColorsToSelect)
        {
            selectedColors[randomIndex] = allColors[i];
        }
    }
    return selectedColors;
}
```
This implementation is using the reservoir sampling algorithm to randomly select a specified number of colors from the input list of colors(allColors) without shuffling the entire list.
It starts by initializing an empty list(selectedColors) and filling it with the first N (numberOfColorsToSelect) elements of the allColors list.
Then, for each subsequent element, it generates a random number between 0 and the current element's index, and if that number is less than N, it replaces an element in the selectedColors list with the current element. This way, the elements in the selectedColors list are a random subset of the entire allColors list.
