To implement a multiple choice dialogue with branching options, you can use a recursive approach where the available choices depend on the previous choice. Here is an example of how you can do this using a `HashMap` in the `Character` class:
```
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.HashMap;

public class Character {
  private String name;
  private HashMap<Integer, HashMap<Integer, String>> dialogue;

  public Character(String name) {
    this.name = name;
    this.dialogue = new HashMap<>();
  }

  public void addDialogue(int choice, int subChoice, String response) {
    if (!dialogue.containsKey(choice)) {
      dialogue.put(choice, new HashMap<>());
    }
    dialogue.get(choice).put(subChoice, response);
  }

  public String talk() {
    Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
    String response = "";
    while (true) {
      System.out.println("Choose a question:");
      for (int choice : dialogue.keySet()) {
        System.out.println(choice + ". " + dialogue.get(choice).get(0));
      }
      int choice = scanner.nextInt();
      if (dialogue.containsKey(choice)) {
        HashMap<Integer, String> subDialogue = dialogue.get(choice);
        while (true) {
          System.out.println("Choose a sub-question:");
          for (int subChoice : subDialogue.keySet()) {
            System.out.println(subChoice + ". " + subDialogue.get(subChoice));
          }
          int subChoice = scanner.nextInt();
          if (subDialogue.containsKey(subChoice)) {
            response = subDialogue.get(subChoice);
            break;
          } else {
            System.out.println("Invalid choice!");
          }
        }
        break;
      } else {
        System.out.println("Invalid choice!");
      }
    }
    return response;
  }
}
```
This `Character` class has a `name` field, a `dialogue` `HashMap`, and a `talk` method that allows the player to choose a question and receive a response from the character. The `addDialogue` method can be used to add choices and responses to the `dialogue` `HashMap`, with the first choice representing the main question and the second choice representing a sub-question.

