```cpp
std::vector<char> save_ciphertext_to_memory(const Ciphertext &ciphertext)
{
    std::ostringstream oss(std::ios::binary);
    ciphertext.save_members(oss);

    // Get the string from the ostringstream
    std::string data_str = oss.str();

    // Convert the string to a vector<char>
    std::vector<char> memory_buffer(data_str.begin(), data_str.end());

    return memory_buffer;
}
```
This function takes a `Ciphertext` object as input and saves it to a `std::vector<char>` using the `save_members` function. The `std::ostringstream` object is used as the output stream to write the data into memory.

