For each edge in the priority queue, the method checks whether the vertex at the other end of the edge has been visited. If not, it adds the edge to the maximum spanning tree and marks the vertex as visited. It then adds all edges incident to the newly visited vertex to the priority queue.

The method assumes that the graph is connected. If the graph is not connected, it will find the maximum spanning tree of one of the connected components.

