If you want to send an SMS instead of creating a call log, you can use the Close.io API to create a new SMS message. You'll need to have a Close.io phone number that supports SMS. Here's the modified script that sends an SMS to the contact with the given phone number:
```php
<?php
require 'vendor/autoload.php';

use GuzzleHttp\Client;

// Configuration
$apiKey = 'YOUR_CLOSE_IO_API_KEY'; // Replace with your Close.io API key
$phoneNumber = 'PHONE_NUMBER'; // Replace with the phone number of the contact you want to send an SMS to
$fromPhoneNumber = 'YOUR_CLOSE_IO_PHONE_NUMBER'; // Replace with your Close.io phone number that supports SMS
$message = 'Hello from Close.io!'; // Replace with the SMS message you want to send

// Prepare Guzzle client for Close.io API
$client = new Client([
    'base_uri' => 'https://api.close.com/api/v1/',
    'headers' => [
        'Content-Type' => 'application/json',
        'Accept' => 'application/json',
        'Authorization' => 'Bearer ' . $apiKey,
    ],
]);

// Search for the contact by phone number
try {
    $searchParams = [
        'query' => 'phone:"' . $phoneNumber . '"',
    ];
    $response = $client->get('contact/', ['query' => $searchParams]);
    $responseData = json_decode($response->getBody(), true);

    // Check if a contact was found
    if ($responseData['total_results'] > 0) {
        $contactId = $responseData['data'][0]['id'];

        // Create a new SMS
        $smsData = [
            'contact_id' => $contactId,
            'from' => $fromPhoneNumber,
            'to' => $phoneNumber,
            'body' => $message,
        ];

        // Execute the API request to send the SMS
        $response = $client->post('activity/sms/', ['json' => $smsData]);
        $responseData = json_decode($response->getBody(), true);

        if ($response->getStatusCode() == 201) {
            echo "SMS sent successfully. SMS ID: " . $responseData['id'] . PHP_EOL;
        } else {
            echo "Error sending SMS. HTTP status code: " . $response->getStatusCode() . ". Response: " . $response->getBody() . PHP_EOL;
        }
    } else {
        echo "No contact found with phone number: $phoneNumber" . PHP_EOL;
    }
} catch (\GuzzleHttp\Exception\RequestException $e) {
    echo "Error: " . $e->getMessage() . PHP_EOL;
}
?>
```
Replace `'YOUR_CLOSE_IO_API_KEY'` with your actual Close.io API key, `'PHONE_NUMBER'` with the phone number of the contact you want to send an SMS to, and `'YOUR_CLOSE_IO_PHONE_NUMBER'` with your Close.io phone number that supports SMS.

The script first searches for the contact with the given phone number, then sends the SMS if the contact is found.

